ext":"The policy rate is 26.5%, so the real policy rate is roughly +11%, which is very high. The next MPC is expected to want clearer evidence of sustained disinflation before cutting, even though the case for easing has strengthened.","src":[]}]},"external":{"as_of":"2026-09-22","points":[{"text":"This is the standout. Gross reserves rose $12.76bn year-on-year to $54.61bn as of 14 September 2026, a 30.5% increase, and they are already above the CBN's full-year projection of about $51.04bn.","src":["Nairametrics"]},{"text":"The naira strengthened from about ₦1,368/$ at end-July to around ₦1,315/$ in early September.","src":["Nairametrics"]}]},"fiscal":{"as_of":"2026-09-22","points":[{"text":"This is the weak spot, and the interest/revenue metric captures it. Based on the 2026–28 MTEF, annualised 2025 revenue of about N23.43trn compared with debt service of N16.26trn, a debt service-to-revenue ratio of about 61%.","src":["Nairametrics"]}]},"debt":{"as_of":"2026-09-22","points":[{"text":"Total public debt was N166.79trn at 30 June 2026, of which 54.91% was domestic.","src":["Nairametrics"]},{"text":"Nigeria has no IMF programme. Moody's has upgraded it to B3.","src":["Trading Economics"]}]},"valuation":{"as_of":"2026-09-22","points":[{"text":"On the DMO sheet dated 22 September, yields run from 5.749% on the Nov 2027 bond to 8.206% on the Sep 2051. The Feb 2032 yields 6.837% and the Dec 2034 yields 7.403%.","src":["DMO"]}]},"catalysts":{"as_of":"2026-09-22","points":[{"text":"The next MPC: a first cut depends on clearer evidence of sustained disinflation.","src":[]}]}},"narrative_pending":false,"derived":{"interest":{},"policy_source":"CBN","policy_rate":["2026-09-22",26.5],"real_rate":3.49,"fx_changes":{"1w":0.15,"1m":-0.0,"3m":-3.08,"1y":-10.1,"ytd":-8.87},"auto":{"macro":["World Bank real GDP growth: 4.0% in 2025 (IMF WEO unavailable on this run).","World Bank CPI inflation: 23.0% in 2025 (IMF WEO unavailable on this run).","Policy rate 26.50% (2026-09-22); real ra